WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.750
(speaks in foreign language)

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.790
- This was the first time
I saw the rainbow flag

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:11.503
raised in my home country, Egypt.

00:00:12.009 --> 00:00:15.759
(speaks in foreign language)

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:20.090
I knew this was going
to be a defining moment

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.403
for the LGBT community in Egypt.

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:25.723
I needed to know who was brave
enough to raise the flag.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.180
But it didn't take long for me to realize

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.383
this action had serious consequences.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.280
- [Reporter] Egyptian authorities
have arrested seven people

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.773
for allegedly holding up a
rainbow flag at a rock concert.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:38.760
- I first reached out
to Ahmed when I learned

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.710
he was being tracked by the government.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:43.763
His name and his face
were all over the news.

00:00:43.789 --> 00:00:47.539
(speaks in foreign language)

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.573
Ahmed had no choice but to hide,

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.890
while the government was
encouraging the media

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.040
to highlight these arrests
to win popular support.

00:00:56.193 --> 00:00:59.943
(speaks in foreign language)

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.193
On October 1st 2017,

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.850
I learned Ahmed was
arrested and put to jail.

00:01:33.451 --> 00:01:36.118
(phone ringing)

00:01:36.904 --> 00:01:40.654
(speaks in foreign language)

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.600
I decided to fly out to Canada

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.903
and take him to his first Pride.

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:02.170
It was important to me
that he have a chance

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:04.313
to raise the rainbow flag without fear.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:07.230
His story made me think
about my own journey

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:09.620
and how I left the Middle
East when I was 18.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:12.600
I was able to explore my identity
without being suppressed.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.383
If I was still in Egypt,

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:16.710
I don't know if I
would've raised the flag.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:19.560
He does something a lot of
others are still scared to do.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:34.457
(foreign language)

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.417
(melancholy music)

00:04:51.032 --> 00:04:54.782
(speaks in foreign language)

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.417
(melancholy music)

00:05:17.233 --> 00:05:20.983
(speaks in foreign language)

00:05:38.177 --> 00:05:39.764
(fast tempo music)

00:05:39.764 --> 00:05:43.514
(speaks in foreign language)

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:35.930
Meeting Ahmed made me realize one thing.

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:38.280
The first time I raised the rainbow flag,

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:39.880
I didn't have to fight for it.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:41.700
I just felt like I belonged.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.650
When Ahmed raised the flag
that night of the concert,

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.793
he wanted to proudly exist.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:49.860
Just like everyone else.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:03.270
- Hey, Unsolved is on a new channel.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:04.103
And now your part.

00:07:04.103 --> 00:07:04.970
Subscribe here.
- Subscribe here.

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:06.093
That was my part.

